WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.924 --> 00:00:18.777
Daisy Kaleem walked up to the farmhouse with Finn.

2
00:00:20.038 --> 00:00:21.099
Daisy was nervous.

3
00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:24.722
"We probably shouldn't be here without permission."

4
00:00:29.365 --> 00:00:32.368
Just then a woman hurried around the side of the farmhouse.

5
00:00:34.012 --> 00:00:34.833
"Oh, hello.

6
00:00:34.853 --> 00:00:37.374
I thought I heard a dog.

7
00:00:38.415 --> 00:00:39.256
I'm Jan.

8
00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:41.437
Do you kids live nearby?

9
00:00:42.038 --> 00:00:43.839
My husband and I are new in town.

10
00:00:44.439 --> 00:00:46.200
We bought this little farm a month ago."

11
00:00:48.182 --> 00:00:49.162
Kaleem smiled.

12
00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:51.664
"You work at the library in town, right?

13
00:00:53.065 --> 00:00:53.886
So does my mom.

14
00:00:54.626 --> 00:00:56.247
I met you last week when I was there."

15
00:00:56.267 --> 00:01:00.410
"I remember now," Jan said.

16
00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.692
"Nice to see you again, Kaleem."

17
00:01:04.732 --> 00:01:05.892
Daisy patted Finn.

18
00:01:06.473 --> 00:01:09.274
"Our friend Finn picked up a new scent and led us here.

19
00:01:09.994 --> 00:01:12.755
Do you have any unusual animals on the farm?"

20
00:01:14.095 --> 00:01:14.836
Jan chuckled.

21
00:01:14.856 --> 00:01:19.997
"We brought our newest one home this afternoon.

22
00:01:20.978 --> 00:01:22.338
Would you like to see him?"

23
00:01:22.358 --> 00:01:24.459
"Yes," Daisy said.

24
00:01:25.679 --> 00:01:27.300
Jan led the way around the house.

25
00:01:39.948 --> 00:01:44.070
When they reached the farmyard, Daisy smiled at all the animals there.

26
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:46.871
Some chickens were pecking around.

27
00:01:48.172 --> 00:01:49.832
A cat was sleeping in the sun.

28
00:01:51.213 --> 00:01:53.374
Goats and sheep were playing in a pen.

29
00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.895
Another pen held two miniature donkeys.

30
00:01:58.016 --> 00:02:04.338
A short distance away, there was a lush pasture where two horses and a cow were grazing.

31
00:02:05.879 --> 00:02:07.980
Suddenly Daisy heard a strange sound.

32
00:02:09.436 --> 00:02:10.857
A man appeared from the barn.

33
00:02:12.258 --> 00:02:16.601
He was leading a tall, shaggy creature who was shrieking with alarm.

34
00:02:17.622 --> 00:02:18.682
Kaleem gasped.

35
00:02:18.702 --> 00:02:24.126
"Is that a "Meet our new llama, Floyd!"

36
00:02:24.806 --> 00:02:25.627
Jan grinned.

37
00:02:25.647 --> 00:02:27.688
"Isn't he cute?"

38
00:02:28.869 --> 00:02:33.052
Now Daisy knew exactly what "monster" the animals had seen!

39
00:02:34.273 --> 00:02:37.315
Floyd was enormous, with a very long neck.

40
00:02:37.735 --> 00:02:39.136
His expression was sour.

41
00:02:39.924 --> 00:02:41.105
He shrieked again.

42
00:02:41.125 --> 00:02:45.509
"I don't hear any words from him," Daisy thought.

43
00:02:45.529 --> 00:02:48.092
"I think it's because he's so upset."

44
00:02:52.416 --> 00:02:55.098
somebody tell that thing to be quiet?"

45
00:02:55.518 --> 00:02:57.520
the cat said, waking up from her nap.

46
00:02:58.621 --> 00:03:02.004
The man was struggling to lead the llama toward the donkeys' pen.

47
00:03:02.024 --> 00:03:05.528
"That's my husband, Jon," Jan said.

48
00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.743
"It looks like he's having trouble with Floyd."

49
00:03:12.264 --> 00:03:15.066
Daisy wondered why the llama was so upset.

50
00:03:17.268 --> 00:03:21.171
While Kaleem asked Jan about the donkeys, Daisy slipped away.

51
00:03:30.339 --> 00:03:33.902
me," she whispered over the fence of the goat and sheep pen.

52
00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:36.324
"Do you like living on this farm?"

53
00:03:36.928 --> 00:03:40.089
The goat looked surprised that Daisy was talking to him.

54
00:03:40.629 --> 00:03:42.330
But he answered her question.

55
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:43.970
"We love it!

56
00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.831
Our people feed us good food.

57
00:03:48.591 --> 00:03:51.032
And look at this rock pile they made for us to play on."

58
00:03:53.593 --> 00:03:54.573
He bounded away.

59
00:03:55.613 --> 00:03:57.554
That was enough to convince Daisy.

60
00:03:58.294 --> 00:04:00.895
This was a nice farm where animals were happy.

61
00:04:01.455 --> 00:04:05.176
She had to convince Floyd to calm down and tell her what was wrong.

62
00:04:06.524 --> 00:04:08.866
"I might be able to help," Daisy said.

63
00:04:08.886 --> 00:04:12.528
"I'm, uh, good with animals.

64
00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:17.031
Hello, Floyd."

65
00:04:17.611 --> 00:04:18.712
The llama looked away.

66
00:04:18.732 --> 00:04:22.235
"You're very cute," Daisy said softly.

67
00:04:23.515 --> 00:04:29.279
As she stepped closer to Floyd, Finn barked, "Don't get too close to that monster!"

68
00:04:29.299 --> 00:04:32.221
"Who are you calling a monster?"

69
00:04:32.501 --> 00:04:33.482
the llama snapped.

70
00:04:34.222 --> 00:04:36.284
He spat out a wad of saliva.

71
00:04:37.064 --> 00:04:38.728
"Stay back, you noisy mutt!"

72
00:04:40.712 --> 00:04:44.821
Suddenly Floyd took off, ripping the rope out of Jon's hands!
